thread:
maria: Quick note from onboarding the new react-starter: error objects are wildly inconsistent across SDKs. Go returns map[string]interface{} with "error_type", JS throws ApiError with only message+status, Python has typed exceptions with retryable attr. This is surprising for users.

jon: Oof. We should pick a canonical surface and normalize per-SDK. Idea: export an ErrorKind enum + normalized fields on all errors: status_code:int, kind:string (one of ErrorKind), retryable:bool, retry_after_ms:Optional[int], raw_body:string. That keeps language idioms but consistent semantics.

kevin: Agreed. Also propose middleware layer in each SDK called `normalizeErrors()` that translates HTTP responses and streaming final envelopes into the canonical error object before handing to callers. That will help sync vs streaming clients.

claire: For mapping: 429 -> ErrorKind.RATE_LIMIT (includeRetryAfter), 401 -> ErrorKind.AUTH (action=reauth), 403 -> ErrorKind.PERMISSIONS, 408/504 -> ErrorKind.NETWORK, 5xx -> ErrorKind.SERVICE. We should encode an explicit `retry_hint` string too: "immediate", "exponential", "none".

maria: Example JS snippet I wrote for docs draft: 

```
// js: normalized errors
try {
  await client.chat.send({ text: 'hi' })
} catch (err) {
  // all SDKs should expose these fields
  if (err.kind === 'RATE_LIMIT') {
    await backoff(err.retry_after_ms || 1000)
  } else if (err.kind === 'AUTH') {
    showReauthDialog()
  } else if (err.retryable) {
    // generic transient retry
    await retryWithExpBackoff()
  } else {
    throw err
  }
}
```

kevin: For Go we can't throw, but pattern: return typed error implementing `NormalizedError() NormalizedErrorShape` so callers can do: `if ne, ok := errors.As(err, &NormalizedError{}); ok { if ne.Kind == RATE_LIMIT { ... } }`. Will add helper `IsRetryable(err)`.

claire: Parity test idea: small CI job in each SDK that runs a mocked server returning known status/header combos and asserts the SDK surface matches the contract JSON (status->kind, fields present). Fail CI if exports or attributes missing.

maria: Also let's update sample apps to show handling for partial streaming responses: display partial output but show a dismissible error banner if the final envelope is an error. That reduces silent failures.

ci-bot: New draft PR: https://git.redwood/rdw/sdk-error-contracts/pull/42 (created by maria)

jon: One more UX nit: error messages should be short and actionable. Avoid dumping full stack into message. Put raw response into `raw_body` so dev tools can surface it but UIs should use `message` + `retry_hint`.

kevin: I'll add the normalizeErrors middleware to the JS SDK PR and a small integration test. Claire can you add the table to docs?

claire: Yup, adding an `errors.md` section with the mapping + code snippets and a checklist for SDK PRs.

maria: Cool. Let's meet for 20m tomorrow to pick exact enum names and whether `retry_after_ms` is required vs optional. 10:30?

jon: Works for me.

